WEBVTT

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:04.046
It's my favorite TV family,

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:04.046
the Griffins.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.673
(all gasping)

00:00:05.715 --> 00:00:06.925
Victory is mine!

00:00:07.717 --> 00:00:08.801
(exclaiming)

00:00:07.717 --> 00:00:08.801
Go on, get out!

00:00:08.843 --> 00:00:10.135
(screaming)

00:00:10.177 --> 00:00:10.929
Housekeeping.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.347
Bing bong!

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.347
Mommy! Mama!

00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:14.390
You're a phony.

00:00:14.432 --> 00:00:15.391
Meg?

00:00:15.433 --> 00:00:16.392
(yelling)

00:00:15.433 --> 00:00:16.392
(gasps)

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:17.602
(retching)

00:00:18.728 --> 00:00:19.144
What do you want,

00:00:18.728 --> 00:00:19.144
a Cleveland steamer?

00:00:19.186 --> 00:00:20.062
All right.

00:00:20.104 --> 00:00:22.565
Bringing the

00:00:20.104 --> 00:00:22.565
good news today?

00:00:22.607 --> 00:00:23.775
It's gonna rain!

00:00:23.816 --> 00:00:25.526
(laughs) Yes!

00:00:25.568 --> 00:00:26.569
No...

00:00:26.611 --> 00:00:27.904
(laughing)

00:00:29.405 --> 00:00:30.322
(giggling)

00:00:30.364 --> 00:00:31.449
Ah, that's right!

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:39.498
I think at one point, I thought

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:39.498
we would get to 200 episodes,

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:40.792
and then when we got canceled,

00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:43.544
I thought, "No, we won't get

00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:43.544
to 200 episodes."

00:00:43.586 --> 00:00:45.546
And then, when we came back,

00:00:45.588 --> 00:00:47.339
I thought, "Yeah, maybe

00:00:45.588 --> 00:00:47.339
we'll get to 200 episodes."

00:00:47.381 --> 00:00:49.759
And now, it's like,

00:00:47.381 --> 00:00:49.759
"Oh, crap, 200 episodes."

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:51.343
I'm so proud of you.

00:00:51.385 --> 00:00:52.804
Way to go, Dad.

00:00:52.845 --> 00:00:54.346
Yeah, you're

00:00:52.845 --> 00:00:54.346
a smart fella, Dad.

00:00:54.388 --> 00:00:56.515
And you're

00:00:54.388 --> 00:00:56.515
a fart smeller, Meg.

00:00:56.557 --> 00:00:57.391
(farts)

00:00:56.557 --> 00:00:57.391
(screams)

00:00:57.433 --> 00:00:58.434
(laughs)

00:00:58.476 --> 00:01:00.352
Wait. We've been on for 200

00:00:58.476 --> 00:01:00.352
episodes?

00:01:00.394 --> 00:01:02.730
Wow. I'm actually almost...

00:01:02.772 --> 00:01:06.025
What I've done is

00:01:02.772 --> 00:01:06.025
I wanted my weight

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.152
to equal how many

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.152
episodes we have.

00:01:08.193 --> 00:01:10.822
So I'm almost, I'm just about

00:01:08.193 --> 00:01:10.822
at 200 pounds.

00:01:10.863 --> 00:01:14.158
And I plan to continue

00:01:10.863 --> 00:01:14.158
to rise with the episodes.

00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:19.330
So, if the show goes 500

00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:19.330
episodes, I will not be able

00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:19.330
to leave my house.

00:01:20.581 --> 00:01:22.082
(beeping)

00:01:24.335 --> 00:01:25.544
I've always found it really

00:01:24.335 --> 00:01:25.544
funny

00:01:25.586 --> 00:01:28.506
and I was excited when

00:01:25.586 --> 00:01:28.506
so many other people did

00:01:28.547 --> 00:01:30.382
'cause it meant that

00:01:28.547 --> 00:01:30.382
all have in common.

00:01:30.424 --> 00:01:31.425
We all find this funny.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:34.345
This is a show

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:34.345
that has never tried

00:01:34.386 --> 00:01:36.514
to be anything more

00:01:34.386 --> 00:01:36.514
than something that

00:01:36.555 --> 00:01:40.351
makes you laugh as often

00:01:36.555 --> 00:01:40.351
and as loudly as possible

00:01:40.392 --> 00:01:42.227
within the course

00:01:40.392 --> 00:01:42.227
of a half hour.

00:01:48.442 --> 00:01:49.819
(screaming)

00:01:49.861 --> 00:01:53.531
(bleeping)

00:01:53.572 --> 00:01:54.448
Damn it!

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:56.450
Oh, my God.

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:56.450
Peter, are you okay?

00:01:56.492 --> 00:01:58.410
No! I am not okay.

00:01:58.452 --> 00:01:59.954
Nothing about

00:01:58.452 --> 00:01:59.954
this is okay.

00:01:59.996 --> 00:02:02.414
Inherently, like, in the show's

00:01:59.996 --> 00:02:02.414
DNA,

00:02:02.456 --> 00:02:05.417
has the ability to go a lot of

00:02:02.456 --> 00:02:05.417
different directions.

00:02:05.459 --> 00:02:09.588
We could tell conventional

00:02:05.459 --> 00:02:09.588
family stories that are

00:02:05.459 --> 00:02:09.588
very character driven.

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:11.173
I say it's four o'clock,

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:11.173
away with you.

00:02:11.215 --> 00:02:12.466
Stewie!

00:02:11.215 --> 00:02:12.466
Change it back!

00:02:12.508 --> 00:02:14.343
No, forget it.

00:02:12.508 --> 00:02:14.343
<i>Jolly Farm Revue</i> is on.

00:02:14.385 --> 00:02:16.345
It's the latest

00:02:14.385 --> 00:02:16.345
indoctrinating pabulum

00:02:16.387 --> 00:02:17.471
for children with

00:02:16.387 --> 00:02:17.471
not enough to do.

00:02:17.513 --> 00:02:20.516
Hey! Shut up.

00:02:20.558 --> 00:02:22.393
And also, you could tell

00:02:20.558 --> 00:02:22.393
buddy comedy.

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:23.769
You could do

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:23.769
buddy comedy episodes

00:02:23.811 --> 00:02:25.730
with Peter and Quagmire

00:02:23.811 --> 00:02:25.730
and Joe.

00:02:25.771 --> 00:02:28.607
Would you rather get

00:02:25.771 --> 00:02:28.607
a massage from a man

00:02:28.649 --> 00:02:31.569
or surgery from

00:02:28.649 --> 00:02:31.569
a female doctor?

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:32.904
Wow!

00:02:32.945 --> 00:02:34.238
<i>And then, beyond that,</i>

00:02:34.279 --> 00:02:37.909
Stewie's got this sort of

00:02:34.279 --> 00:02:37.909
scientific bent where

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:41.412
it opens the door

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:41.412
to tell all kinds of

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:41.412
sci-fi stories.

00:02:41.453 --> 00:02:43.789
Da Vinci must be

00:02:41.453 --> 00:02:43.789
my ancestor.

00:02:43.831 --> 00:02:45.207
Good Lord!

00:02:45.249 --> 00:02:47.126
That's who Bertram's

00:02:45.249 --> 00:02:47.126
here to kill.

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.669
So, that means

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.669
you're Italian.

00:02:48.711 --> 00:02:51.505
Of course,

00:02:48.711 --> 00:02:51.505
my love for SpaghettiO's

00:02:48.711 --> 00:02:51.505
and smoking on the toilet.

00:02:51.547 --> 00:02:53.173
It all makes sense.

00:02:53.215 --> 00:02:57.553
You know, it really helps

00:02:53.215 --> 00:02:57.553
having all those avenues

00:02:53.215 --> 00:02:57.553
to pursue.

00:02:57.595 --> 00:03:01.432
Creatively, I've always said

00:02:57.595 --> 00:03:01.432
come to writing<i> Monty Python,</i>

00:03:01.473 --> 00:03:02.975
where any funny idea

00:03:01.473 --> 00:03:02.975
that you have

00:03:03.017 --> 00:03:06.729
you can somehow fit it

00:03:03.017 --> 00:03:06.729
into an episode of<i> Family Guy.</i>

00:03:06.771 --> 00:03:09.815
It doesn't even

00:03:06.771 --> 00:03:09.815
have to serve the story

00:03:06.771 --> 00:03:09.815
as long as it's funny enough.

00:03:09.857 --> 00:03:12.443
I got something

00:03:09.857 --> 00:03:12.443
for you here.

00:03:09.857 --> 00:03:12.443
What is it?

00:03:12.484 --> 00:03:14.445
I caught you

00:03:12.484 --> 00:03:14.445
